commit e8b5e27350ddc9f2a928d9337e0431b241d85187
Author: billy needham <billyluisneedham@duck.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 20 20:43:34 2026 +0100

    console: add the resolver agent and merge-approval to the pool engine
    
    When a merge conflicts, spawn the resolver agent (resolver= or the
    ~/.issue-runner default) in the parked worktree to stage a resolution,
    then present it as a merge-approval interrupt before any commit. Approve
    commits the resolution and continues; reject converts to a manual
    merge-conflict interrupt carrying the agent's attempt; a failing resolver
    takes the same manual path. Merge-kind interrupts are exempted from the
    rehydrate stale-clearing so a pending approval survives a restart.
    
    PoolRun gains approve() and reject() beside resume(). The resolver harness
    is configurable, defaults to ~/.issue-runner, and names an unknown harness
    fail-fast. Covered by engine-seam tests with real git conflicts and a stub
    resolver.

