The engine is designed so the returned `PoolRun.resume()` returns the next run. So the server can hold the current `PoolRun` and call resume on it. But `runPool` itself returns a promise that resolves when the run reaches a quiescent/done/stalled phase. The `onSnapshot` callback fires on every snapshot. So the server:
