Issue 07 is complete and committed. Here's what was done:

## Summary

**Server** (`engine/server.ts`, `engine/server.test.ts`) — one Bun process per pool:
- Serves the built SPA from `ui/dist`, a JSON API (`/api/state`, `/api/start`, `/api/resume` with optional note), and an SSE stream (`/api/stream`) pushing a full snapshot on every change.
- Drives the engine via `runPool`, enriching each snapshot with ticket metadata (title, blockedBy, marker-derived status) so the projection can draw edges. CLI: `bun run engine/server.ts --pool <dir> [--port <n>]`.

**UI** — rewritten active path (`client.ts`, `project.ts`, `main.ts`, `view.ts`, `styles.css`):
- Tickets render as cards with blocked-by edges; START and REVIEW appear as visually distinct small utility cards; card status mirrors the line-1 marker status live.
- The UI renders from snapshots only, over SSE. Canvas mechanics (pan, zoom, drag, edge-routing toggle, persisted positions) and the Detail panel are unchanged.
- The LangGraph client, thread list, and thread projection are gone from the main path: `data.ts`, `mock.ts`, `variants/VariantC.ts`, and the `@langchain/langgraph-sdk` dependency were deleted (bundle dropped ~68 KB → ~17 KB).

**Testing** — 29 projection tests over snapshot fixtures (following the prior precedent) + 3 server smoke tests.

**Verification** — root + UI typechecks pass, 80 engine/server tests + 29 UI tests pass, `vite build` succeeds, and an end-to-end smoke (serve SPA, get state, SSE, close) confirmed working.

**Issue file** — all 8 acceptance criteria ticked, `status=done`, with Notes and a Brief written. Committed as `716b7ab`. Inline interrupt-answering forms are deliberately deferred to Issues 08 and 09; this Issue exposes the `/api/resume` endpoint they build on.
